** Workshop exercise 04: quarter of a simplified four-layer cable section under external pressure (our own deck).
** TEACHING SIMPLIFICATION: plane strain, bonded linear-elastic homogeneous layers, illustrative material values.
** Units: N, mm, MPa. Needs cable_mesh.inp (Gmsh output with CPS6 renamed to CPE6) and cable_pressure_load.inc
** (one *DLOAD line per outer element face); see README.md.
*INCLUDE, INPUT=cable_mesh.inp
*MATERIAL, NAME=COPPERLIKE
*ELASTIC
110000., 0.34
*MATERIAL, NAME=POLYMERLIKE
*ELASTIC
1000., 0.45
*MATERIAL, NAME=ALUMINIUMLIKE
*ELASTIC
70000., 0.33
*MATERIAL, NAME=STEELLIKE
*ELASTIC
210000., 0.30
*SOLID SECTION, ELSET=CORE, MATERIAL=COPPERLIKE
1.
*SOLID SECTION, ELSET=INSULATION, MATERIAL=POLYMERLIKE
1.
*SOLID SECTION, ELSET=SHEATH, MATERIAL=ALUMINIUMLIKE
1.
*SOLID SECTION, ELSET=ARMOUR, MATERIAL=STEELLIKE
1.
*STEP
*STATIC
*BOUNDARY
SYMX, 1
SYMY, 2
*INCLUDE, INPUT=cable_pressure_load.inc
*NODE PRINT, NSET=P_CORE
U
*NODE PRINT, NSET=P_OUTER
U
*NODE FILE
U
*EL FILE
S
*END STEP
